 "title": "Welcome to Cottonwood County, MN",
 "text": "Welcome to Cottonwood County, MN\nSkip to main content\nOctober 18, 2026 | 11:35 am | 58°\nGovernment\nGovernment Information\nData Practices\nMission Statement\nSocial Media Policy\nCounty Commissioners\n1st District\n2nd District\n3rd District\n4th District\n5th District\nBoard Meeting Information\nBoard Meeting Agendas & Minutes\nCity Officials\nTownship Officials\nDepartments\nAdministrative\nAssessor\nAuditor/Treasurer\nCounty Attorney\nCounty Ditches\nHuman Resources\nInformation Systems\nRecorder\nCourts & Legal\nCourt Administration\nLaw Library\nProbation\nSheriff\nCounty Elected Officials\nAuditor/Treasurer\nCounty Attorney\nCounty Commissioners\nRecorder\nSheriff\nServices\nEmergency Management\nEnvironmental Office\nExtension\nFamily Services\nHighway\nParks\nSolid Waste And Recycling\nVeterans\nResidents\nLiving & Working In Cottonwood County\nCounty Holidays\nCounty Maps\nFAQ\nHelpful Links\nJob Opportunities\nNews\nCounty Parks\nFamily Services\nSheriff\nVeterans Services\nWaste & Recycling Services\nVisitors\nAbout Cottonwood County\nCounty Maps\nTalcot Park Campground\nI Want To\nApply For / Obtain\nBirth Certificates\nBuilding Permit\nDeath Certificates\nDrivers License\nJob Opportunities\nMarriage License\nPassports\nRead / Download\nAssessor Applications & Forms\nBoard Meeting Agendas & Minutes\nPlanning Applications & Forms\nTreasurer Forms\nFind / Learn About\nAssessor FAQ\nCounty Board Meeting Info\nEmergency Management FAQ\nHighway FAQ\nProbation FAQ\nRecorder FAQ\nSheriff FAQ\nSolid Waste/Recycling FAQ\nReport / Request\nRequest Appointment\nRequest Transportation\nContact Us\nSearch\n1\n2\n3\n4\nPrev Next\nMinutes & Agendas\nJob Openings\nOnline Services\nPay your bills\nPark & recreation\nWelcome to Cottonwood County\nCottonwood County is located in the southwestern part of the state of Minnesota. Our current population is 12,167 with an area of 636 square miles. Our county seat is the city of Windom.\nCottonwood County was organized July 29, 1870. It was named for the Cottonwood River, which touches the northeast corner of Germantown Township in Cottonwood County. The river was named for the abundance of cottonwood trees on its banks.\nAt the time of the organization, Minnesota Governor Austin appointed three county commissioners. Their first meeting was held at a private home located about six miles northwest of Windom on the Des Moines River at Big Bend. At this meeting, the commissioner districts were designated and various county officers were changed. The first general election was held in the fall of 1870 so some of these officials changed at that time. The first deed on record was filed January 10, 1870 and the first land assessments were made in 1871. The first taxes were paid in 1872.\nClick here for the 2026 Cottonwood County Information Guide\nRecent News\nJuly 30, 2026\nCottonwood County hires new Public Works Director\nMarch 23, 2023\nWelcome to Cottonwood County, Minnesota\nCottonwood County is located in the southwestern part of the state of Minnesota. Our current population is 12,167 with an area of 636 square miles. Our county seat is the city of Windom.\nTo read more about Cottonwood County, click here .\nTo see Cottonwood County's location on a map, click here .\nEmergency Management\nPublic Works\nSheriff\nShare this page\n×\nShare this page\nCopy and paste this code into your website.\n<a href=\"http://www.cottonwoodcountymn.gov/\">Your Link Name</a>\nShare this page on your favorite Social network\nFacebook\nTwitter\nReddit\nClose\n×\nVeterans Service Officer Hired\nCottonwood County has hired a new Veterans Service Officer.\nRead More\nPowered by Revize , the Government Website Experts | Login\n© 2020 Cottonwood County\n|\nContact Us",
